# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools path traversal via PackageIndex/easy_install's
# download-to-tmp-then-extract flow. Present in the OS-level setuptools bundled
# by ghcr.io/platform-base-images/python-base, including the latest available
# release (1.0.15) as of 2026-08-31 — no patched base image exists yet.
# Not exploitable here: python-api only runs `pip install -r requirements.txt`
# against a fully pinned lockfile at build time; nothing in the app or its
# runtime invokes setuptools' package-download/extraction path.
# Tracked upstream in platform-base-images/hardened-base. Remove this line once
# a python-base release without this finding is available.
CVE-2025-47273

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack out-of-bounds read/crash on Unpacker reuse
# after an error. Same situation: an OS-level python package bundled by
# python-base (installed 1.1.2, fixed 1.2.1), not a dependency of python-api
# (msgpack does not appear in requirements.txt) and not imported by the app.
# Tracked upstream in platform-base-images/hardened-base; remove once fixed.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
